@startuml
title Connection Lifecycle - Redis-like Server

[*] --> Admission : TCP connection accepted

Admission --> Rejected : past --maxclients
Rejected --> [*] : "-ERR max number of clients reached", closed

Admission --> Waiting : admitted

state Waiting : wait for bytes;\n--idle-timeout runs here
state Parsing : cut complete requests\nout of the buffer
state Executing : run the batch, a command at a time;\n--request-timeout runs from here
state Writing : send every reply\nof the batch at once

Waiting --> Parsing : bytes read
Parsing --> Waiting : no complete request yet
Parsing --> Executing : one or more requests
Executing --> Writing : replies ready
Writing --> Waiting : all sent

Waiting --> Closed : client closed, idle limit,\nquery buffer past its limit
Executing --> Closed : request limit (batch dropped\nif still queued)
Writing --> Closed : protocol error (after its reply),\noutput past its limit, request limit
Waiting --> Closed : server shutting down

Closed --> [*]

@enduml
